// ============================================================================
// Forgepoint AI Gateway Proto Definitions (M7 — LLMOps)
// ============================================================================
//
// The AI Gateway is the LLM analogue of the Inference Gateway: one entry point
// that fronts many model backends ("providers") and applies the cross-cutting
// concerns every production LLM system needs — provider routing + FAILOVER
// (circuit breaker), per-tenant TOKEN BUDGETS (rate limiting), a semantic CACHE,
// streaming, and usage/cost metering. The model itself is deliberately tiny
// (a local Ollama smollm2); the subject is the platform infrastructure.
//
// PATTERN REUSE: every concern here maps to a pattern already
// built elsewhere in Forgepoint —
//   - provider failover      -> Circuit Breaker (inference-gateway)
//   - per-team token budgets  -> distributed Rate Limiter (inference-gateway)
//   - prompt/model A-B + canary -> Traffic Splitting (model-serving)
//   - token cost metering     -> Outbox reliable events (billing)
//   - streaming tokens        -> server-streaming gRPC -> BFF SSE
//
// REAL-WORLD COMPARISON: LiteLLM / Portkey / Cloudflare AI Gateway (routing +
// caching) — but those are thin on deep cost attribution + governance, which
// Forgepoint already has (billing outbox, audit log, model-monitor).
// ============================================================================

